# The basic rotation around Arcane (Array Arcana: INT).
#
# Built for one account: roster/endfield.profile.yaml, snapshot of
# 2026-09-03. Skill levels, weapons and gear are real, not defaults.
#
#   Arcane    sk.12/12/12/12  Junction Point r1       Hot Work ×3 + LYNX Slab
#   Tangtang  sk.10/11/11/10  Brigand's Calling r1    Bonekrusha ×3 + MI Security
#   Xaihi     sk.3/10/9/12    Detonation Unit r1      Eternal Xiranite ×3, P5
#   Perlica   sk.3/11/12/9    Stanza of Memorials r4  Pulser Labs ×3, P5
#
# THE MAIN RULE: Arcane comes in LAST.
#
# All of the team's damage hangs on Corrosion, and it only happens when Nature
# Infliction lands ON Cryo stacks already built. The order decides the reaction:
#
#   Nature ON Cryo  →  Corrosion       (resistance shred to EVERY element)
#   Cryo ON Nature  →  Solidification  (freeze, no shred)
#
# If Arcane applies Nature too early, Tangtang's next Waterspout produces
# Solidification, the Cryo stacks burn away, and there is no Corrosion this cycle.
#
# THE SECOND RULE: Arcane's combo goes BEFORE her battle skill, not after.
#
# The combo trigger of the INT form has two branches:
#   "When Nature Infliction OR at least 2 stacks of non-Nature Arts Infliction
#    are applied on an enemy"
# The second branch means two Cryo stacks from Xaihi and Tangtang are already
# enough, and there is NO NEED to spend her own Nature Infliction to arm the combo.
#
# The combo itself does not use up the Cryo stacks: it deals Nature DMG but
# applies only Susceptibility, not Infliction. The stacks survive until the
# battle skill.
#
# So the battle skill AFTER the combo does two things in one cast:
#   - the first Nature Infliction lands on the built Cryo  → Corrosion;
#   - the hit lands on a target under Imprisonment         → the signature bonus
#     (30 SP back, a 120% burst, a 500% bonus, a second Susceptibility instance).
# The order "battle → combo → battle" would waste an extra 100 SP per cycle.
#
# The Imprisonment window is 4 s, and that limit decides WHAT to hold back.
# Hold the COMBO, not the battle skill: the combo is armed at 2 Cryo stacks
# already, and stays armed as long as the stacks are up (Arts Infliction lasts
# 20 s). After the combo there are only 4 seconds for everything, no time to
# build stacks inside that window.
#
# Corrosion's Status Level = the number of stacks eaten. With the talent
# Weapon Honing E3 (×1.1) and Hot Work ×3 (Arts Intensity +30 → ×1.18) the
# shred tops out at:
#   2 stacks → −20.8 and 240% ATK on the initial hit
#   3 stacks → −26.0 and 320%
#   4 stacks → −31.2 and 400%
# The ramp to the cap takes 10 s regardless of level.
#
# How many stacks to build DEPENDS ON THE ENCOUNTER, and this was checked in a fight:
#
#   boss, one big target  →  build to 4 and dump it into a shared window with the ultimates.
#     The −31.2 shred stays up for 25 s and multiplies the whole burst, not one
#     cast. The 10 s Corrosion ramp pays off, because the target lives that long.
#
#   waves of small enemies →  combo and battle skill right away at 2 stacks.
#     Corrosion is back-loaded: its value is in the 10-second ramp, and small
#     enemies die before the shred grows. Tempo and AOE matter more here:
#     Tangtang's battle skill with 3 pillars and Arcane's AOE grid clear a wave
#     faster than deep Corrosion on one target.
#
# There are only two sources of Cryo, and both give exactly one stack per cast
# (Tangtang's data says so outright: "once per skill cast"), so the 4th stack
# costs a separate cast — that pays off on a boss, not on waves.

# Perlica: NEVER press her battle skill. It applies Electric Infliction, which
# eats the Cryo stacks and produces Electrification instead of Corrosion. Her
# combo applies Electrification FORCIBLY, and forced reactions do not consume
# stacks — so the combo is safe, and the battle skill breaks the whole cycle.

title: Arcane corrosion: Arcane / Tangtang / Xaihi / Perlica
team: Arcane, Tangtang, Xaihi, Perlica
# ===========================================================================
variant: waves
# Many small targets. No waiting for stacks or for the Corrosion ramp — tempo,
# AOE and frequent battle skills from Tangtang for clearing matter more.
# ===========================================================================

Tangtang: BS
# Open the fight with her: at the start there is no Cryo Infliction on the
# target, and Tangtang's combo needs "applying Cryo Infliction OR dealing Arts
# Burst DMG" — nothing can arm it until the battle skill has landed. The first
# Waterspout applies Cryo.

Tangtang: CS
# Now the trigger is met. Whirlpool + a Bonekrusha stack
# (set ×3: the next battle skill +30%, up to 2 stacks).

Tangtang: BS
# Eats the Whirlpool → extra Waterspouts: this is the main AOE clear.
# Arts Susceptibility, the Brigand's Calling debuff, SP back, and Cryo stacks
# on everyone within the radius.

Xaihi: BS
Arcane: BA > FS
Perlica: CS
Arcane: BA > FS
Xaihi: CS
# A second Cryo stack on the target + Arts Burst. Arcane's combo is armed.

Arcane: CS
# Hits the target AND nearby enemies — on a wave it lands on several at once.

Arcane: BS
# Corrosion SL II (−20.8). Small, but nothing more is needed here: the
# Jadecrushing Grid is AOE, and it finishes off the pack.

Arcane: BA > FS

cycle 2:
Tangtang: CS > CS
Tangtang: BS
Arcane: CS > BS
Xaihi: ULT~
# Press Xaihi's ultimate if it is charged: Amp ~31% and Eternal Xiranite +16% to the team.

# ===========================================================================
variant: boss
# One big target. Build to 4 stacks and dump everything into one window.
# ===========================================================================

Xaihi: BS
Tangtang: BS
Tangtang: CS
Arcane: BA > FS
Perlica: CS
Arcane: BA > FS
Xaihi: CS
# Cryo stack #2 + Arts Burst.

Tangtang: CS
Tangtang: BS
# Stack #3, three pillars, Arts Susceptibility 9%, 40 SP back.

Tangtang: ULT
Arcane: DIVE
# The cheap way to the 4th stack. Talent Riot Bringer E3: a dive attack during
# OLDEN STARE ends the spin early and creates a Waterspout, and every Whirlpool
# nearby turns into extra ones. These pillars have the same effects as those
# from the battle skill (so they apply Cryo Infliction) and get DMG Dealt +60%.
# Plus an early Rogue Wave at 599% instead of 342% and Stagger 20 instead of
# 15 — that is the contribution to the stagger window.

Arcane: ULT
# IMPORTANT: put the array down IN ADVANCE, before the stagger window. It lasts
# 20 s and is not going anywhere. Casting it inside the window loses seconds
# on the wind-up. On creation: 180% damage, Stagger 10, forced Corrosion and
# Arts Amp 24% on Arcane from talent E2.

Perlica: ULT
# 800% and Stagger 20 — fills the stagger bar. Plus Stanza of Memorials r4:
# casting the ultimate gives operators of OTHER elements ATK +12.8% for 20 s.
# Arcane, Tangtang and Xaihi are all non-Electric, so the buff lands on all three.
# Perlica's P5 adds Crit Rate +30% to her ultimate.

Xaihi: ULT
# The last of the buffers, right before the burst: the Amp window is only 12 s.
# Cryo and Nature Amp ~31% + Eternal Xiranite ×3 → the team gets +16% damage for 15 s.

Arcane: CS
# The combo at 4 Cryo stacks. Imprisonment for 4 s, Nature and Cryo Susceptibility.

Arcane: BS
# Corrosion STATUS LEVEL IV: an initial hit of 400% ATK and a shred cap of
# −31.2 on every element for 25 s. At the same time — the signature bonus on
# the target under Imprisonment (30 SP, a 120% burst, a 500% bonus) and the
# Hot Work window, +50% Nature.

Arcane: FIN
Arcane: FIN
# THIS SOLVES CHARGING THE ULTIMATE'S SECOND HIT.
# The Cluster Strike trigger: "hitting an enemy within the Gloompurger Array
# with a Finisher OR a Final Strike". A finisher is a basic attack on a
# STAGGERED enemy, which is exactly what the stagger window offers.
# Two finishers charge both stages of Cluster Strike many times faster than
# two full five-hit chains up to a Final Strike. And the finisher itself hits
# for 900% ATK and returns SP.

Arcane: ULT
# Gloompurge Arcana — 1440%, in a window of Corrosion IV, Xaihi's Amp, ATK
# from Perlica's ultimate, Hot Work +50% and both Susceptibilities.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT CHECK
#
# Written before the simulation counted resources. On SP: cycle 1 spends 400 SP
# (Xaihi 100, Tangtang 200, Arcane 100) and gets 70 back → 330 net. Natural
# regeneration is ~8 SP/s, so ~41 s of pure regen. Final Strikes cover the
# difference, and that is why the BA > FS steps here are not decoration but
# part of the economy.
# The order "combo → battle" saves exactly 100 SP per cycle against
# "battle → combo → battle": a whole extra cast somewhere else.
#
# There are no "this gives +N% damage" figures here on purpose: they come
# from the damage track now, not from a hand count.
